From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:05:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] media: mediatek: add MT6878 seninf + CAMSV raw capture

Raw Bayer capture for MT6878 without the ISP: CSI port 2 (C-PHY, three
trios) -> SENINF_5 -> seninf mux 0 -> cammux 10 -> CAMSV2 tag 2 IMGO, the
route stock uses for the rear sensor. The register sequences follow the
isp7sp seninf driver (CSI PHY 3.1) and the CAMSV programming that
libccd composes into its command queue; FIFO thresholds and the PHY
efuse word are the values read back on stock.

The media graph is sensor -> seninf subdev -> camsv video node, with the
platform driver named "mtk-seninf" for the libcamera simple pipeline.
IMGO runs in UNPACK_MODE, which stores the 8 MSBs of each RAW10 pixel,
so the node offers 8-bit Bayer. Buffers are scatter-gather pages mapped
into the MM M4U, one IOVA slot per buffer index; without a queued buffer
the frame buffer controller drops frames.

camsys_main has no clock driver yet, so the camera gates are opened by
register here. CAM_MAIN and CSI_RX are runtime-PM power domains.
